// Lead Pro -- popup.js  v9.7.375-dev (DEV. Same vehicle-gate warn disambiguation as 9.7.373 Commercial (see that entry) — warn now states VEHICLE PRESENT AND BLOCKED vs no-vehicle-in-rescue-data, so a genuinely vehicle-less Gubagoo lead can never again masquerade as a gate failure. All measurement diagnostics remain active; F1 gate still included pending validation. Builds on v9.7.374-dev / v9.7.373.)
// Lead Pro -- popup.js  v9.7.374-dev (DEV. Same rescue-provenance SECOND-STAGE FIX as 9.7.372 Commercial (see that entry) — the rescued object now carries the vehicle-supplying frame's autoLeadId/dealerId so the v9.7.371 gate verifies real data instead of always seeing none/none on the rescue path. All measurement diagnostics ([LP STABILITY DIAG], [LP DOM-VERIFY DIAG]) remain active; F1's PASS-2 anti-bleed gate still included pending validation batch. Builds on v9.7.373-dev / v9.7.372.)
// Lead Pro -- popup.js  v9.7.373-dev (DEV — MEASUREMENT BUILD. Adds [LP DOM-VERIFY DIAG] at the rescue path: fire-and-forget scan of all lead-like frames (rims2/CustomerDashboard/frameploader) logging, per frame, whether the beacon's active lead ID appears ANYWHERE in the frame's DOM (document.documentElement.innerHTML.indexOf) alongside whether the three known marker locations found an ID. Purpose: test the candidate verification signal for the unverifiable-frame VOI block (the Angelle case — rescue frame with no autoLeadId AND no dealerId stays vehicle-blocked fail-safe under v9.7.371's refined gate). If the signal proves reliable across real grabs — active ID present in the DOM of correct frames, absent in stale/wrong ones — it becomes the gate that safely allows vehicle merge from marker-less frames, and it naturally defeats the repeat-customer trap (an old lead's frame contains the OLD id, not the active one) that made name/phone identity matching unsafe for gating a lead-level fact like vehicle. Runs at rescue time specifically because that is the exact moment the real fix would evaluate. NOTE: the stability-check fix direction is DEAD — first real data from 9.7.372-dev (two grabs) proved a stale frame can point at the wrong lead STABLY for the entire 6s window (everChanged:false on a wrong-lead baseline), so consistency-based verification would confidently confirm the wrong answer; the beacon was correct in that same grab, reinforcing beacon-as-ground-truth. runStabilityDiagnostic remains in this build for continued settle-time collection but no fix will be built on stability alone. Observes only, gates nothing. Builds on v9.7.372-dev.)
// Lead Pro -- popup.js  v9.7.372-dev (DEV. Three changes: (1) Same v9.7.371 vehicle-gate REGRESSION FIX as Commercial (see that entry in the 9.7.371 Commercial build) — positive-mismatch/verified-dealer rule replaces the too-aggressive mismatch-or-missing block that was silently killing VOI pickup on ordinary rescue grabs. (2) Fable-review finding 2c fix, completed: the stability diagnostic now establishes its comparison baseline from its OWN first frame-based read instead of the committed initialWinnerId — on beacon/URL-resolved grabs those come from different measurement instruments, and comparing across instruments logged spurious "CHANGED" events on exactly the most common navigation path, which would have systematically polluted the settle-time data. Cross-instrument disagreement is now logged once as an informational note, never counted as instability. (3) Fable-review finding 2b fix: the diagnostic's in-frame collector now includes the hidden-input AutoLeadID fallback matching the real pre-scrape's recovery capability — without it, frames the real path successfully IDs came back ID-less in polls, changing candidate counts and producing artifact winner-flips. Diagnostic data gathered on 9.7.371-dev should be DISCARDED — it predates fixes 2 and 3 and is unreliable; collect fresh on this build. Builds on v9.7.371-dev / v9.7.371.)
// Lead Pro -- popup.js  v9.7.371-dev (DEV — MEASUREMENT BUILD, no fix, no behavior change. Adds runStabilityDiagnostic(), a fire-and-forget background loop that fires AFTER the real pre-scrape (runPreScrape, completely untouched) has already committed window._activeLeadId via the existing Strategy 0-4 logic. For ~6 seconds after every grab, re-reads frame candidates every 300ms and logs [LP STABILITY DIAG] lines: whether the winning lead ID ever changes after the real commit point, when the LAST change happened, and the final settled winner. This is purely observational — it never writes to window._activeLeadId or any variable the real generation pipeline reads (verified: grepped every window._activeLeadId assignment in the file, confirmed the new functions contain none). Purpose: replace the assumed settle-time distribution used in the stability-check latency simulation (discussed but not yet built as a real fix) with real measured data from actual use, before locking in any delay/retry-count constants. The winner-selection logic in computeWinnerFromFrameCandidatesDiagOnly is intentionally DUPLICATED from runPreScrape rather than shared, specifically so this measurement code can never alter the real production path even during a future edit. DEV-only — no reason to ship the extra scripting calls and console noise to agents; this exists to gather data, not to change behavior. Remove once enough real-world settle-time data has been collected. scraperVersion stays v9.7.51. Builds on v9.7.370-dev.)
