      // (v9.7.498/493 — SELF-CONSISTENCY: WHAT WE HAVE ALREADY TOLD THIS CUSTOMER)
      // Steph Montoya (Honda Baytown) is the clearest case yet: LP said the K5 was "here and
      // ready for you to see" on 6/24, said it "has sold" on 6/29, said "already sold" on 7/2 —
      // and on 7/27 asked whether she is "still focused on the K5 GT". Three separate patches
      // this week (trade conflation, sold re-announcement, in-place record correction) were all
      // the same underlying problem treated locally: every generation reads the thread fresh with
      // no notion of what LP has ALREADY ASSERTED, so it contradicts or re-announces its own
      // claims. Rather than another local rule, capture the claims themselves and put them in
      // front of the model as its own commitments, newest last, so contradicting one is a visible
      // act rather than an accident. OUTBOUND ONLY — a customer saying "is it still available?"
