      // logged "truncated 965 chars", which is exactly what made this hard to see: it cut at a
      // marker FURTHER ALONG the entry (Total CRM entries:) and left the unrecognised EXIT
      // SIGNAL block standing, so the log reported success while the directive still shipped.
      // A truncation count is not proof the entry came out clean.
      // Two additions: the glyph-less headers that were missing by name, and a STRUCTURAL family
      // rule for Lead Pro's directive glyphs followed by an uppercase header. The glyph rule is
      // what stops this being a list that silently rots every time a directive is added — the
      // failure mode this exact bug is. 🔥 is deliberately matched only in "🔥 LIVE CONVERSATION"
      // rather than joining the glyph class, because customers genuinely text 🔥 in caps.
      var _scaffoldRe = /\s*(?:FOLLOW-UP: read the full transcript|AGENT CONTEXT — READ THIS FIRST|Total CRM entries:|MOST RECENT CUSTOMER MESSAGE|CONVERSATION TRANSCRIPT \(|IDENTIFIED CUSTOMER CONCERNS|CUSTOMER COMMITMENTS \/ OPEN ITEMS|CRITICAL: Your response MUST|EXIT SIGNAL:|PAUSE SIGNAL:|VEHICLE\/LEAD DETAILS:|VEHICLE ON LEAD:|PRESENCE LANGUAGE:|CRM ENGAGEMENT RATING:|VEHICLE PIVOT DETECTED:|INVENTORY \(|RULES FOR THIS RESPONSE:|⚠ STALLED LEAD:|🚫 ZERO-CONTACT LEAD|🔥 LIVE CONVERSATION|(?:⚠|📅|🔑|✅|🧾|☎|🎯|🚚|🚫|📋|🆕)\uFE0F?\s*[A-Z]{2,})/;
